---
const team = [
  { name: 'Architect', role: 'Planner', exp: 'Senior · Staff · Principal', color: '#b794f4' },
  { name: 'Builders', role: 'Executors', exp: 'Mid-level to senior', color: '#67e8f9' },
  { name: 'Reviewers', role: 'Semantic gate', exp: 'Senior ICs', color: '#fbbf24' },
  { name: 'PAT', role: 'Continuous assurance', exp: 'Hybrid QA / engineering', color: '#86efac' },
  { name: 'Junior', role: 'Apprenticeship', exp: 'Pairing + PAT participation', color: '#7cc4ff' },
];

const ratios = [
  'Reviewer capacity ≥ Builder capacity',
  '≥ 2 Planner-eligible per Domain',
  '~1 PAT per 3–5 active Builder seats',
];
---

<div class="card p-6 md:p-8">
  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-1">A balanced GI team per domain</div>
    <div class="text-sm text-muted">Reviewer capacity is the throughput ceiling. Sizing follows ratios, not fixed counts.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
    {ratios.map((r) => (
      <div class="card p-3 text-xs font-mono text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <span class="text-accent">→</span> {r}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-5">
    {team.map((t) => (
      <div class="card p-4 flex flex-col" style={`border-top: 3px solid ${t.color};`}>
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">{t.role}</span>
        <div class="mt-2 text-base font-medium" style={`color: ${t.color}`}>{t.name}</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted leading-snug">{t.exp}</div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="mt-5 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
    Role names describe <em>modes of work</em>, not job titles. A certified engineer can pick up Builder or Reviewer tasks on Tracks they hold the right cert for, subject to per-artifact separation of duties.
  </div>
</div>
